    },
    {
      "id": "with-two-auth-tokens",
      "description": "SUBSCRIBE carrying AUTHORIZATION_TOKEN twice, with different Token Values. The parameter's own definition is the carve-out: \"The AUTHORIZATION TOKEN parameter MAY be repeated within a message as long as the combination of Token Type and Token Value are unique after resolving any aliases.\" The second instance is written as a Type Delta of 0, which is the only encoding a second instance has once Section 10.2 requires ascending order. Identical to the with-auth-token-use-value vector with the count raised and a second token appended, so the only new bytes are the repeat itself.",
      "hex": "0300340101046c69766505766964656f02031103006d792d6265617265722d746f6b656e001103006d792d62656172652d7365636f6e64",
      "decoded": {
